      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexia%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Texas and Central Railroad arrived in 1871, Mexia transformed into a bustling railroad town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofmexia.com/218/City-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1922, Mexia briefly fell under martial law as its rapid growth overwhelmed local authorities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexia%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Confederate Reunion Grounds State Historic Site, a 70‑acre park, hosted Confederate veterans each year from 1889 to 1946.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
